"""
QCar 1 - Autonomous Perpendicular Parking
=========================================

Two modes:

  --mode vehicles   Parking next to parked vehicles.
                    Drives forward along a row of parked cars (noses facing the
                    aisle), uses the side LiDAR beam to find a gap wide enough
                    for the QCar, computes the spot center, and parks in it.
                    While entering, it uses the neighbors on both sides to stay
                    centered.

  --mode empty      Parking in an empty parking lot (no reference vehicles).
                    Drives forward looking at the floor with the side CSI camera
                    on --side, detects taped stall lines (undistort -> bird's-eye
                    view -> color threshold -> HoughLinesP), finds an adjacent
                    pair of lines spaced STALL_WIDTH apart, confirms it over
                    several frames, then parks in that stall. LiDAR is still used
                    for safety and to stop at a curb/wall at the back of the spot.

Entry direction (both modes):  --entry reverse (default) | forward
Spot side (both modes):        --side right (default) | left

State machine:
    GYRO_CAL  (both)     hold still ~2 s, estimate gyro z bias
    SEARCH    (vehicles) creep forward, find a LiDAR gap of sufficient width
              (empty)    creep forward, find a camera-detected stall
    POSITION  drive straight forward/back to the turn start point
    TURN      90 deg arc at full steering lock toward the spot
    ENTER     straight into the spot with heading hold (+ centering in vehicles mode)
    DONE      stop, hazards on
    ABORT     refused / gave up (reason printed), stop, hazards on

Geometry (rear-axle point follows a circle of radius R = WHEELBASE / tan(MAX_STEER)):
    reverse-in: start the turn with the rear axle R *past* the spot center
    forward-in: start the turn with the rear axle R *before* the spot center
    after the 90 deg arc the rear axle sits R deep (laterally) from the start line.

Hardware / software:
    Quanser QCar 1 (or virtual QCar in QLabs), Quanser PAL python library, OpenCV.
    Sensors: RPLidar (QCarLidar), motor tachometer, IMU gyroscope, side CSI camera.

PAL API assumptions (NOT verified against your PAL version - check them):
    - QCar.motorTach is the car's linear speed in m/s, signed (+ forward).
      Some PAL versions/QCar models expose motor-shaft speed instead; if so the
      odometry will be scaled wrong. See "encoder scale" in the measurement list.
    - QCar.gyroscope is [x, y, z] in rad/s.
    - QCarLidar.read() may block until a new scan arrives (~10 Hz on the RPLidar)
      or may return immediately with the last scan, depending on PAL version.
      The loop integrates with measured dt, so either behavior is handled; the
      once-per-second timing log shows which one you have.
    - QCar(readMode=0) does immediate (non-task-based) I/O on each read_write_std.
    - PAL's QCar class is primarily documented for QCar 2; confirm it supports
      your QCar 1 (older code used Quanser.product_QCar / q_essential instead).
    - QCarCameras(frameWidth, frameHeight, frameRate, enableRight, enableLeft, ...)
      exposes .csiRight / .csiLeft Camera2D objects whose .read() refreshes
      .imageData (HxWx3 uint8, assumed BGR). The return value of read() and
      whether it blocks are not verified; duplicate frames are filtered out.
      The camera ID -> physical side mapping may differ on QCar 1: confirm with
      --calibrate-camera that "right" really shows the right side.

Camera calibration files (per side, OpenCV FileStorage YAML, paths in config):
    intrinsics:  model ("pinhole" | "fisheye"), image_width, image_height
                 (= the capture size the calibration was done at), K (3x3), D.
    bird's-eye:  H (3x3) mapping UNDISTORTED pixels at PROC_SIZE resolution
                 (exactly what --calibrate-camera saves as *_undistorted.png)
                 to BEV pixels; proc_width, proc_height; bev_width, bev_height;
                 meters_per_px; origin_fwd_m, origin_out_m = floor position of
                 BEV pixel (0,0) relative to the camera's ground point.
                 BEV convention: column -> +forward, row -> +outward (away from
                 the car), so row 0 is the edge nearest the car.

Usage:
    python qcar_self_parking.py --calibrate
    python qcar_self_parking.py --calibrate-camera --side right
    python qcar_self_parking.py --mode vehicles
    python qcar_self_parking.py --mode vehicles --entry forward --side left
    python qcar_self_parking.py --mode empty --entry reverse --side right

ALWAYS test with the car on a stand first, then at low speed with a hand on
the e-stop. Ctrl+C stops the car immediately.
"""

import argparse
import math
import os
import signal
import sys
import time

import cv2
import numpy as np

from pal.products.qcar import QCar, QCarLidar, QCarCameras


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Configuration  (tune these for your car / track)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SCRIPT_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))

# --- QCar 1 geometry [m] ---
CAR_LENGTH = 0.425
CAR_WIDTH = 0.192
WHEELBASE = 0.256
REAR_OVERHANG = 0.085          # rear bumper -> rear axle
LIDAR_FROM_REAR_AXLE = 0.13    # lidar is this far ahead of the rear axle
MAX_STEER = 0.5                # [rad] QCar steering limit (+ = left)

# derived
TURN_RADIUS = WHEELBASE / math.tan(MAX_STEER)                 # ~0.47 m (verify by measurement)
CENTER_FROM_REAR_AXLE = CAR_LENGTH / 2.0 - REAR_OVERHANG      # geometric center offset
LIDAR_TO_FRONT_BUMPER = CAR_LENGTH - REAR_OVERHANG - LIDAR_FROM_REAR_AXLE
LIDAR_TO_REAR_BUMPER = REAR_OVERHANG + LIDAR_FROM_REAR_AXLE

# --- Control loop / timing ---
SAMPLE_RATE = 100              # [Hz] target rate; real rate may be lower if lidar.read() blocks
DT = 1.0 / SAMPLE_RATE         # target period (used only for sleeping, not for integration)
DT_MAX = 0.2                   # [s] clamp on measured dt so a hiccup can't cause a big jump
TIMING_LOG_PERIOD = 1.0        # [s] how often to print average / max loop time
MAX_RUN_TIME = 120.0           # [s] hard timeout

# --- Gyro bias calibration (car stationary, zero throttle) ---
GYRO_CAL_DURATION = 2.0        # [s] averaging window
GYRO_CAL_MAX_STD = 0.01        # [rad/s] above this the car was probably bumped/moving
GYRO_CAL_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3      # give up (abort) after this many noisy attempts

# --- Speeds [m/s] ---
SEARCH_SPEED = 0.20            # vehicles-mode LiDAR search
STALL_SEARCH_SPEED = 0.12      # empty-mode camera search (slower: less blur, more frames per stall)
POSITION_SPEED = 0.15
TURN_SPEED = 0.12
ENTER_SPEED = 0.08

# --- Speed PI controller (throttle command is roughly -1..1) ---
KP_SPEED = 0.15
KI_SPEED = 0.8
MAX_THROTTLE = 0.20            # keep this low while testing

# --- Heading hold / centering while entering the spot ---
K_HEADING = 1.5                # [rad steer / rad heading error]
K_CENTER = 1.0                 # [rad steer / m lateral error] (vehicles mode)
MAX_CORRECTION_STEER = 0.20
TURN_ARC_TOLERANCE = 1.3       # abort arc if odometry exceeds 1.3x expected arc length

# --- LiDAR angle convention ---
# Run --calibrate and hold your hand in front of / right of the car to check.
# FRONT_ANGLE_DEG: raw lidar angle that points straight ahead.
# ANGLE_DIR: +1 if raw angles increase counter-clockwise (toward left), -1 if clockwise.
FRONT_ANGLE_DEG = 0.0
ANGLE_DIR = -1
LIDAR_MAX_VALID = 5.0          # [m] readings beyond this (or 0) are treated as "no return"

# --- Gap detection (vehicles mode) ---
SIDE_SECTOR_HALF_WIDTH = 3.0   # [deg] around the 90 deg side beam
GAP_DEPTH_JUMP = 0.20          # [m] side distance must grow by this much to count as a gap
SPOT_SIDE_MARGIN = 0.10        # [m] required clearance on each side of the car
MIN_GAP_WIDTH = CAR_WIDTH + 2 * SPOT_SIDE_MARGIN   # ~0.39 m
MAX_GAP_WIDTH = 3.0 * CAR_WIDTH                    # wider than this = open space; use first part
ENTRANCE_MARGIN = 0.03         # [m] how far past the neighbors' bumpers to pull in

# --- Search limits (both modes) ---
MAX_SEARCH_DISTANCE = 3.0      # [m] give up if no usable gap / stall found within this distance
ROW_DETECT_MAX_DIST = 1.5      # [m] (vehicles) side return closer than this counts as "a parked car"

# --- Row clearance guard (vehicles mode) ---
# The single-arc maneuver must finish turning before the leading bumper crosses
# the neighbors' bumper line. Leading-bumper depth at the end of the arc:
#   reverse-in: TURN_RADIUS + REAR_OVERHANG
#   forward-in: TURN_RADIUS + (CAR_LENGTH - REAR_OVERHANG)
# The car refuses to park if the row is closer than that depth + this margin.
ROW_CLEARANCE_MARGIN = 0.05    # [m]

# --- Camera capture / preprocessing (empty mode) ---
CAMERA_CAPTURE_SIZE = (820, 410)   # (w, h) requested from the CSI camera; intrinsics must match
CAMERA_FPS = 30
CAMERA_COLOR_ORDER = "BGR"         # "BGR" or "RGB" - order of Camera2D.imageData (unverified)
PROC_SIZE = (320, 240)             # (w, h) frames are downscaled to this before undistort/BEV.
                                   # K is scaled per axis, so a different aspect than capture is OK.
CAMERA_INTRINSICS_FILE = {
    "right": os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, "calib", "csi_right_intrinsics.yaml"),
    "left": os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, "calib", "csi_left_intrinsics.yaml"),
}
CAMERA_BEV_FILE = {
    "right": os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, "calib", "csi_right_bev.yaml"),
    "left": os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, "calib", "csi_left_bev.yaml"),
}
FISHEYE_BALANCE = 0.0          # fisheye model: 0 = crop to valid pixels, 1 = keep full FOV
PINHOLE_ALPHA = 0.0            # pinhole model: same idea, for getOptimalNewCameraMatrix
# Camera ground point (point on the floor directly below the lens) in the car frame:
#   (forward of rear axle [m], outward from car centerline toward that side [m]).  MEASURE.
CAMERA_MOUNT = {
    "right": (0.13, 0.095),
    "left": (0.13, 0.095),
}
CAMERA_LATENCY_S = 0.0         # [s] capture -> processing delay; odom is back-dated by speed*latency

# --- Stall-line detection (empty mode) ---
TAPE_HSV_LOW = (0, 0, 180)     # default: white/bright tape. Tune with --calibrate-camera.
TAPE_HSV_HIGH = (180, 60, 255)
MORPH_KERNEL_PX = 3            # opening kernel to remove speckle
HOUGH_THRESHOLD = 20           # accumulator votes
HOUGH_MIN_LINE_LENGTH = 0.06   # [m] shortest segment HoughLinesP returns
HOUGH_MAX_LINE_GAP = 0.03      # [m] gap HoughLinesP may bridge
LINE_ANGLE_TOL_DEG = 15.0      # keep segments within this of perpendicular to travel
LINE_MERGE_DIST = 0.04         # [m] segments closer than this along the aisle = same tape line
MIN_LINE_EXTENT = 0.10         # [m] a tape line must be visible over at least this lateral length
ENTRANCE_EDGE_MARGIN_PX = 3    # line's near end must be this far from the BEV's near valid edge
                               # (otherwise the stall entrance is cut off and can't be located)
ENTRANCE_ALIGN_TOL = 0.05      # [m] the two lines' near ends must agree this well
STALL_WIDTH = 0.40             # [m] center-to-center spacing of the two stall lines.  MEASURE.
STALL_WIDTH_TOL = 0.05         # [m]
STALL_DEPTH = 0.60             # [m] stall length from entrance to back.  MEASURE.
STALL_CONFIRM_FRAMES = 5       # consecutive frames the same stall must be seen before committing
STALL_MAX_MISSES = 0           # frames without a match tolerated inside a run (0 = strictly consecutive)
STALL_MATCH_TOL = 0.05         # [m] along-aisle agreement for "same stall" between frames
STALL_MATCH_TOL_LATERAL = 0.05 # [m] lateral agreement for "same stall" between frames

# --- --calibrate-camera helper ---
CAMCAL_OUTPUT_DIR = os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, "camera_calib_frames")
CAMCAL_NUM_FRAMES = 10
CAMCAL_INTERVAL = 1.0          # [s] between saved frames

# --- Safety ---
SAFETY_STOP_DIST = 0.08        # [m] bumper clearance that triggers a stop
SAFETY_SECTOR_HALF_WIDTH = 15.0

# --- Heading sign ---
# +1 if gyroscope[2] is positive when the car turns LEFT (CCW). Verify on a stand.
GYRO_Z_SIGN = 1

# --- LEDs (QCar has 8). Verify indices on your car. ---
LED_LEFT_IND = (0, 2)
LED_RIGHT_IND = (1, 3)
LED_BRAKE = (4, 5)
LED_HEAD = (6, 7)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Helpers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def wrap_deg(a):
    return (a + 180.0) % 360.0 - 180.0


class LidarView:
    """Wraps QCarLidar and gives distances in car-frame sectors.
    Car-frame angle: 0 = front, +90 = left, -90 = right, 180 = rear."""

    def __init__(self):
        self.lidar = QCarLidar(numMeasurements=720,
                               rangingDistanceMode=2,
                               interpolationMode=0)
        self.car_angles = None
        self.dist = None

    def update(self):
        # NOTE: may block until a new scan is available, or may return the
        # previous scan immediately - depends on the PAL version (unverified).
        self.lidar.read()
        raw_deg = np.degrees(np.asarray(self.lidar.angles, dtype=float))
        self.car_angles = wrap_deg(ANGLE_DIR * (raw_deg - FRONT_ANGLE_DEG))
        d = np.asarray(self.lidar.distances, dtype=float).copy()
        d[(d <= 0.02) | (d > LIDAR_MAX_VALID)] = np.inf
        self.dist = d

    def sector(self, center_deg, half_width_deg, stat="min"):
        if self.dist is None:
            return np.inf
        diff = np.abs(wrap_deg(self.car_angles - center_deg))
        vals = self.dist[diff <= half_width_deg]
        vals = vals[np.isfinite(vals)]
        if vals.size == 0:
            return np.inf
        return float(np.min(vals) if stat == "min" else np.median(vals))

    def front(self):
        return self.sector(0.0, SAFETY_SECTOR_HALF_WIDTH)

    def rear(self):
        return self.sector(180.0, SAFETY_SECTOR_HALF_WIDTH)

    def side(self, side_sign):
        """side_sign +1 = right, -1 = left"""
        return self.sector(-90.0 * side_sign, SIDE_SECTOR_HALF_WIDTH, stat="median")

    def terminate(self):
        self.lidar.terminate()


class SpeedController:
    def __init__(self):
        self.integral = 0.0

    def reset(self):
        self.integral = 0.0

    def step(self, target, measured, dt):
        if target == 0.0:
            self.reset()
            return 0.0
        err = target - measured
        self.integral = float(np.clip(self.integral + err * dt, -0.3, 0.3))
        u = KP_SPEED * err + KI_SPEED * self.integral
        u += 0.04 * np.sign(target)          # feed-forward to overcome stiction
        return float(np.clip(u, -MAX_THROTTLE, MAX_THROTTLE))


def leds(left=False, right=False, brake=False, head=True):
    arr = np.zeros(8)
    if left:
        arr[list(LED_LEFT_IND)] = 1
    if right:
        arr[list(LED_RIGHT_IND)] = 1
    if brake:
        arr[list(LED_BRAKE)] = 1
    if head:
        arr[list(LED_HEAD)] = 1
    return arr


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Side camera + stall-line detection (empty mode)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

class SideCamera:
    """One side CSI camera via PAL QCarCameras. read() returns a new frame or None."""

    def __init__(self, side, dedupe=True):
        # ASSUMPTION: argument names / attributes as in PAL's QCarCameras (unverified on QCar 1)
        self.cams = QCarCameras(frameWidth=CAMERA_CAPTURE_SIZE[0],
                                frameHeight=CAMERA_CAPTURE_SIZE[1],
                                frameRate=CAMERA_FPS,
                                enableRight=(side == "right"),
                                enableLeft=(side == "left"))
        self.cam = self.cams.csiRight if side == "right" else self.cams.csiLeft
        self.dedupe = dedupe
        self._prev_sig = None

    def read(self):
        ok = self.cam.read()
        img = self.cam.imageData
        if ok is False or img is None or getattr(img, "size", 0) == 0:
            return None
        if self.dedupe:
            # read() may hand back the previous frame if no new one has arrived;
            # skip exact repeats so one frame can't count twice toward confirmation.
            sig = img[::32, ::32].copy()
            if self._prev_sig is not None and sig.shape == self._prev_sig.shape \
                    and np.array_equal(sig, self._prev_sig):
                return None
            self._prev_sig = sig
        return img

    def terminate(self):
        self.cams.terminate()


def _open_fs(path, what):
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        raise FileNotFoundError(
            f"{what} file not found: {path}\n"
            f"See the 'Camera calibration files' section at the top of this script.")
    fs = cv2.FileStorage(path, cv2.FILE_STORAGE_READ)
    if not fs.isOpened():
        raise IOError(f"could not open {what} file: {path}")
    return fs


class StallLineDetector:
    """Undistort + bird's-eye warp (one precomputed remap), tape threshold,
    HoughLinesP, perpendicular-line clustering, and stall-pair matching.
    All outputs are in the CAR frame: fwd = meters ahead of the rear axle,
    out = meters from the car centerline toward the camera's side."""

    def __init__(self, side):
        self.side = side
        self.mount_fwd, self.mount_out = CAMERA_MOUNT[side]
        self._load_intrinsics(CAMERA_INTRINSICS_FILE[side])
        self._load_bev(CAMERA_BEV_FILE[side])
        self._build_maps()
        self.kernel = np.ones((MORPH_KERNEL_PX, MORPH_KERNEL_PX), np.uint8)
        self.hsv_code = cv2.COLOR_RGB2HSV if CAMERA_COLOR_ORDER == "RGB" else cv2.COLOR_BGR2HSV

    # ---- calibration loading / map precomputation ----
    def _load_intrinsics(self, path):
        fs = _open_fs(path, "camera intrinsics")
        self.model = (fs.getNode("model").string() or "pinhole").strip().lower()
        w = int(fs.getNode("image_width").real())
        h = int(fs.getNode("image_height").real())
        K = fs.getNode("K").mat()
        D = fs.getNode("D").mat()
        fs.release()
        if K is None or D is None or w <= 0 or h <= 0:
            raise ValueError(f"{path}: needs model, image_width, image_height, K, D")
        if (w, h) != tuple(CAMERA_CAPTURE_SIZE):
            print(f"[CAM][WARN] intrinsics were calibrated at {w}x{h} but capture is "
                  f"{CAMERA_CAPTURE_SIZE[0]}x{CAMERA_CAPTURE_SIZE[1]} - K is scaled, "
                  f"but only correct if the sensor crop is the same")
        K = K.astype(np.float64).copy()
        K[0, :] *= PROC_SIZE[0] / float(w)     # fx, skew, cx
        K[1, :] *= PROC_SIZE[1] / float(h)     # fy, cy
        self.K = K
        self.D = D.astype(np.float64)

    def _load_bev(self, path):
        fs = _open_fs(path, "bird's-eye homography")
        H = fs.getNode("H").mat()
        proc = (int(fs.getNode("proc_width").real()), int(fs.getNode("proc_height").real()))
        self.bev_w = int(fs.getNode("bev_width").real())
        self.bev_h = int(fs.getNode("bev_height").real())
        self.mpp = float(fs.getNode("meters_per_px").real())
        self.origin_fwd = float(fs.getNode("origin_fwd_m").real())
        self.origin_out = float(fs.getNode("origin_out_m").real())
        fs.release()
        if H is None or self.bev_w <= 0 or self.bev_h <= 0 or self.mpp <= 0:
            raise ValueError(f"{path}: needs H, proc_width/height, bev_width/height, "
                             f"meters_per_px, origin_fwd_m, origin_out_m")
        if proc != tuple(PROC_SIZE):
            raise ValueError(f"{path}: homography was made at {proc[0]}x{proc[1]} but "
                             f"PROC_SIZE is {PROC_SIZE[0]}x{PROC_SIZE[1]} - redo it or change PROC_SIZE")
        self.H = H.astype(np.float64)

    def _build_maps(self):
        size = tuple(PROC_SIZE)
        if self.model == "fisheye":
            D4 = self.D.reshape(-1)[:4].reshape(4, 1)
            K_new = cv2.fisheye.estimateNewCameraMatrixForUndistortRectify(
                self.K, D4, size, np.eye(3), balance=FISHEYE_BALANCE)
            m1, m2 = cv2.fisheye.initUndistortRectifyMap(
                self.K, D4, np.eye(3), K_new, size, cv2.CV_32FC1)
        else:
            K_new, _ = cv2.getOptimalNewCameraMatrix(self.K, self.D, size, PINHOLE_ALPHA, size)
            m1, m2 = cv2.initUndistortRectifyMap(self.K, self.D, None, K_new, size, cv2.CV_32FC1)
        self.und_map1, self.und_map2 = m1, m2

        # Compose undistort + homography into ONE remap from the downscaled raw
        # frame straight to the BEV, so each frame costs a single cv2.remap and
        # only floor pixels inside the BEV region are ever touched.
        cols, rows = np.meshgrid(np.arange(self.bev_w, dtype=np.float32),
                                 np.arange(self.bev_h, dtype=np.float32))
        pts = np.stack([cols, rows], axis=-1).reshape(-1, 1, 2)
        und = cv2.perspectiveTransform(pts, np.linalg.inv(self.H)).reshape(self.bev_h, self.bev_w, 2)
        ux = np.ascontiguousarray(und[..., 0], dtype=np.float32)
        uy = np.ascontiguousarray(und[..., 1], dtype=np.float32)
        self.bev_map_x = cv2.remap(m1, ux, uy, cv2.INTER_LINEAR,
                                   borderMode=cv2.BORDER_CONSTANT, borderValue=-1)
        self.bev_map_y = cv2.remap(m2, ux, uy, cv2.INTER_LINEAR,
                                   borderMode=cv2.BORDER_CONSTANT, borderValue=-1)
        w, h = size
        valid = ((self.bev_map_x >= 0) & (self.bev_map_x <= w - 1) &
                 (self.bev_map_y >= 0) & (self.bev_map_y <= h - 1))
        self.bev_valid = valid.astype(np.uint8) * 255
        # nearest (smallest) valid row per column = near edge of what the camera sees
        any_valid = valid.any(axis=0)
        self.near_valid_row = np.where(any_valid, valid.argmax(axis=0), self.bev_h)

    # ---- coordinate helpers ----
    def _px(self, meters):
        return max(1, int(round(meters / self.mpp)))

    def px_to_car(self, col, row):
        fwd = self.mount_fwd + self.origin_fwd + col * self.mpp
        out = self.mount_out + self.origin_out + row * self.mpp
        return fwd, out

    def car_to_px(self, fwd, out):
        col = (fwd - self.mount_fwd - self.origin_fwd) / self.mpp
        row = (out - self.mount_out - self.origin_out) / self.mpp
        return int(round(col)), int(round(row))

    def undistort(self, small):
        return cv2.remap(small, self.und_map1, self.und_map2, cv2.INTER_LINEAR)

    # ---- detection ----
    def detect(self, frame):
        small = cv2.resize(frame, tuple(PROC_SIZE), interpolation=cv2.INTER_AREA)
        bev = cv2.remap(small, self.bev_map_x, self.bev_map_y, cv2.INTER_LINEAR,
                        borderMode=cv2.BORDER_CONSTANT, borderValue=0)
        hsv = cv2.cvtColor(bev, self.hsv_code)
        mask = cv2.inRange(hsv, np.array(TAPE_HSV_LOW, np.uint8), np.array(TAPE_HSV_HIGH, np.uint8))
        mask = cv2.bitwise_and(mask, self.bev_valid)
        mask = cv2.morphologyEx(mask, cv2.MORPH_OPEN, self.kernel)

        raw = cv2.HoughLinesP(mask, 1, np.pi / 180.0, HOUGH_THRESHOLD,
                              minLineLength=self._px(HOUGH_MIN_LINE_LENGTH),
                              maxLineGap=self._px(HOUGH_MAX_LINE_GAP))
        segs = [] if raw is None else [tuple(int(v) for v in s) for s in raw.reshape(-1, 4)]

        # keep segments roughly perpendicular to travel (= vertical in the BEV)
        kept = []
        for x1, y1, x2, y2 in segs:
            ang = math.degrees(math.atan2(abs(x2 - x1), abs(y2 - y1)))   # 0 = perpendicular
            if ang <= LINE_ANGLE_TOL_DEG:
                kept.append((x1, y1, x2, y2))

        clusters = self._cluster(kept)
        stalls, spacings, rejected_entrance = self._pair(clusters)
        return {"small": small, "bev": bev, "mask": mask, "segs": segs, "kept": kept,
                "clusters": clusters, "stalls": stalls, "spacings": spacings,
                "rejected_entrance": rejected_entrance}

    def _cluster(self, kept):
        items = []
        for x1, y1, x2, y2 in kept:
            f1, o1 = self.px_to_car(x1, y1)
            f2, o2 = self.px_to_car(x2, y2)
            items.append({"fwd": 0.5 * (f1 + f2), "len": math.hypot(f2 - f1, o2 - o1),
                          "near": min(o1, o2), "far": max(o1, o2),
                          "near_row": min(y1, y2), "far_row": max(y1, y2),
                          "col": 0.5 * (x1 + x2)})
        items.sort(key=lambda it: it["fwd"])

        groups = []
        for it in items:
            if groups:
                g = groups[-1]
                g_fwd = sum(i["fwd"] * i["len"] for i in g) / sum(i["len"] for i in g)
                if it["fwd"] - g_fwd <= LINE_MERGE_DIST:
                    g.append(it)
                    continue
            groups.append([it])

        clusters = []
        for g in groups:
            total = sum(i["len"] for i in g)
            near = min(i["near"] for i in g)
            far = max(i["far"] for i in g)
            if far - near < MIN_LINE_EXTENT:
                continue
            col = int(round(sum(i["col"] * i["len"] for i in g) / total))
            col = int(np.clip(col, 0, self.bev_w - 1))
            near_row = min(i["near_row"] for i in g)
            clusters.append({
                "fwd": sum(i["fwd"] * i["len"] for i in g) / total,
                "near": near, "far": far,
                "col": col, "near_row": near_row, "far_row": max(i["far_row"] for i in g),
                "entrance_visible": near_row > self.near_valid_row[col] + ENTRANCE_EDGE_MARGIN_PX,
            })
        return clusters

    def _pair(self, clusters):
        stalls, spacings, rejected_entrance = [], [], 0
        for a, b in zip(clusters, clusters[1:]):
            s = b["fwd"] - a["fwd"]
            spacings.append(s)
            if abs(s - STALL_WIDTH) > STALL_WIDTH_TOL:
                continue
            if not (a["entrance_visible"] and b["entrance_visible"]):
                rejected_entrance += 1
                continue
            if abs(a["near"] - b["near"]) > ENTRANCE_ALIGN_TOL:
                continue
            entrance = 0.5 * (a["near"] + b["near"])
            stalls.append({"fwd": 0.5 * (a["fwd"] + b["fwd"]),
                           "lateral": entrance + STALL_DEPTH / 2.0,
                           "spacing": s})
        return stalls, spacings, rejected_entrance

    # ---- debug drawing (for --calibrate-camera) ----
    def draw(self, det):
        vis = det["bev"].copy()
        invalid = det["bev"].copy()
        invalid[:] = (60, 0, 60)
        vis = np.where(self.bev_valid[..., None] > 0, vis, invalid)
        for x1, y1, x2, y2 in det["segs"]:
            cv2.line(vis, (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (0, 0, 255), 1)          # red: all Hough segments
        for x1, y1, x2, y2 in det["kept"]:
            cv2.line(vis, (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (0, 255, 0), 1)          # green: perpendicular
        for c in det["clusters"]:
            cv2.line(vis, (c["col"], c["near_row"]), (c["col"], c["far_row"]), (255, 0, 0), 2)
            color = (255, 255, 0) if c["entrance_visible"] else (0, 0, 255)
            cv2.circle(vis, (c["col"], c["near_row"]), 3, color, -1)   # cyan = entrance end seen
        for st in det["stalls"]:
            col, row = self.car_to_px(st["fwd"], st["lateral"])
            if 0 <= col < self.bev_w and 0 <= row < self.bev_h:
                cv2.circle(vis, (col, row), 5, (0, 255, 255), 2)       # yellow: stall center
            cv2.putText(vis, f"{st['spacing']:.2f}m", (max(0, col - 20), 12),
                        cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.35, (0, 255, 255), 1)
        bar = self._px(STALL_WIDTH)
        cv2.line(vis, (5, self.bev_h - 6), (5 + bar, self.bev_h - 6), (255, 255, 255), 2)
        cv2.putText(vis, "STALL_WIDTH", (5, self.bev_h - 10),
                    cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.3, (255, 255, 255), 1)
        return vis


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Perpendicular parking state machine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

class PerpendicularParker:
    def __init__(self, mode, entry, side):
        self.mode = mode                      # "vehicles" | "empty"
        self.entry = entry                    # "reverse" | "forward"
        self.side = side
        self.k = 1 if side == "right" else -1 # +1 right, -1 left
        self.dir = -1 if entry == "reverse" else 1

        # load camera calibration before touching hardware, so a missing file fails cleanly
        self.detector = StallLineDetector(side) if mode == "empty" else None
        self.camera = None

        self.car = QCar(readMode=0, frequency=SAMPLE_RATE)
        self.lidar = LidarView()
        if mode == "empty":
            try:
                self.camera = SideCamera(side)
            except Exception:
                self.car.terminate()
                self.lidar.terminate()
                raise
        self.speed_ctrl = SpeedController()

        self.odom = 0.0        # [m] rear-axle path length (signed: + fwd, - rev)
        self.heading = 0.0     # [rad] relative to start, + = left
        self.speed = 0.0
        self.gyro_bias = 0.0   # [rad/s] raw gyroscope[2] at rest
        self._last_t = time.monotonic()
        self.abort_reason = None

        # Spot description in the start frame:
        #   spot_x      = along-aisle position of spot center (odom frame, rear axle)
        #   entry_depth = straight distance to travel after the 90 deg arc
        self.spot_x = None
        self.entry_depth = None
        self.turn_start_x = None

        # Vehicles-mode search
        self.baseline_side = None
        self.gap_start = None
        self.gap_row_dist = None   # distance from car centerline to neighbors' bumpers

        # Empty-mode stall tracking + diagnostics
        self.stall_track = []      # [(x_odom, lateral)] of consecutive matching detections
        self.stall_misses = 0
        self.cam_frames = 0
        self.frames_with_lines = 0
        self.frames_with_stall = 0
        self.frames_entrance_cut = 0
        self.best_spacing = None   # adjacent-line spacing closest to STALL_WIDTH seen so far
        self.best_run = 0

        self.turn_start_odom = None
        self.enter_start_odom = None
        # reverse-in turns the nose away from the spot, forward-in toward it
        self.target_heading = (self.k if entry == "reverse" else -self.k) * math.pi / 2.0

        self.state = "SEARCH"

        self._stop = False
        signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, self._on_sigint)

    def _on_sigint(self, *_):
        print("\n[!] Ctrl+C - stopping")
        self._stop = True

    def _abort(self, reason):
        self.abort_reason = reason
        self.state = "ABORT"
        print(f"[ABORT] {reason}")

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------
    # Planning
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------
    def _turn_start_from_center(self, spot_x):
        # reverse-in: rear axle moves backward R while turning -> start R past center
        # forward-in: rear axle moves forward R while turning -> start R before center
        return spot_x + TURN_RADIUS if self.entry == "reverse" else spot_x - TURN_RADIUS

    def _plan_empty(self, spot_x, spot_lateral):
        """spot_x: stall center along the aisle (odom frame, rear axle).
        spot_lateral: car centerline -> stall center, toward --side."""
        self.spot_x = spot_x
        # After the arc the rear axle is TURN_RADIUS deep. The car's geometric
        # center is CENTER_FROM_REAR_AXLE toward the aisle (reverse-in) or
        # deeper into the spot (forward-in).
        if self.entry == "reverse":
            center_depth_after_arc = TURN_RADIUS - CENTER_FROM_REAR_AXLE
        else:
            center_depth_after_arc = TURN_RADIUS + CENTER_FROM_REAR_AXLE
        self.entry_depth = spot_lateral - center_depth_after_arc
        if self.entry_depth < 0:
            print(f"[WARN] spot_lateral {spot_lateral:.2f} m is closer than the turn allows "
                  f"({center_depth_after_arc:.2f} m). Car will end {-self.entry_depth:.2f} m too deep. "
                  f"Start further from the spot.")
            self.entry_depth = 0.0
        self.turn_start_x = self._turn_start_from_center(self.spot_x)
        print(f"[PLAN] empty lot | R={TURN_RADIUS:.3f} m | spot center x={self.spot_x:.2f} m, "
              f"lateral={spot_lateral:.2f} m | turn at x={self.turn_start_x:.2f} m "
              f"(now {self.odom:.2f}) | enter {self.entry_depth:.2f} m after arc")

    def _leading_bumper_depth_after_arc(self):
        if self.entry == "reverse":
            return TURN_RADIUS + REAR_OVERHANG
        return TURN_RADIUS + (CAR_LENGTH - REAR_OVERHANG)

    def _plan_vehicles(self, gap_start, gap_end):
        """Returns True if a plan was made, False if the maneuver was refused."""
        width = gap_end - gap_start
        # gap edges are already in the odom frame (odom + LIDAR_FROM_REAR_AXLE),
        # so the midpoint is the spot center.
        self.spot_x = 0.5 * (gap_start + gap_end)
        row = self.gap_row_dist

        required = self._leading_bumper_depth_after_arc() + ROW_CLEARANCE_MARGIN
        if row < required:
            self._abort(
                f"row too close for a single-arc {self.entry}-in: row distance {row:.2f} m < "
                f"required {required:.2f} m (leading bumper depth after arc "
                f"{self._leading_bumper_depth_after_arc():.2f} m + margin {ROW_CLEARANCE_MARGIN:.2f} m). "
                f"Drive at least {required:.2f} m from the parked cars' bumpers and retry.")
            return False

        # Pull in until the bumper nearest the aisle is ENTRANCE_MARGIN past the neighbors.
        if self.entry == "reverse":
            # nose faces aisle: front bumper is (CAR_LENGTH - REAR_OVERHANG) ahead of rear axle
            rear_axle_depth = row + ENTRANCE_MARGIN + (CAR_LENGTH - REAR_OVERHANG)
        else:
            # rear faces aisle: rear bumper is REAR_OVERHANG behind rear axle
            rear_axle_depth = row + ENTRANCE_MARGIN + REAR_OVERHANG
        self.entry_depth = max(0.0, rear_axle_depth - TURN_RADIUS)
        self.turn_start_x = self._turn_start_from_center(self.spot_x)
        print(f"[PLAN] gap width {width:.2f} m, row distance {row:.2f} m | "
              f"spot center x={self.spot_x:.2f} m | turn at x={self.turn_start_x:.2f} m "
              f"(now {self.odom:.2f}) | enter {self.entry_depth:.2f} m after arc")
        return True

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------
    # Low level
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------
    def _tick(self):
        """Measured, clamped time since the last integration step."""
        now = time.monotonic()
        dt = min(max(now - self._last_t, 0.0), DT_MAX)
        self._last_t = now
        return dt

    def _integrate(self, dt):
        # ASSUMPTION: motorTach is linear car speed in m/s (see header notes)
        self.speed = float(self.car.motorTach)
        self.odom += self.speed * dt
        gz = float(self.car.gyroscope[2]) - self.gyro_bias
        self.heading += GYRO_Z_SIGN * gz * dt

    def drive(self, target_speed, steering, led_arr):
        dt = self._tick()
        throttle = self.speed_ctrl.step(target_speed, self.speed, dt)
        self.car.read_write_std(throttle=throttle,
                                steering=float(np.clip(steering, -MAX_STEER, MAX_STEER)),
                                LEDs=led_arr)
        self._integrate(dt)

    def stop_car(self, led_arr=None, settle=0.0):
        """Zero throttle for `settle` seconds, still integrating odom/heading
        so any coast-down is counted."""
        self.speed_ctrl.reset()
        if led_arr is None:
            led_arr = leds(brake=True)
        t_end = time.monotonic() + max(settle, 5 * DT)
        while time.monotonic() < t_end:
            dt = self._tick()
            self.car.read_write_std(throttle=0.0, steering=0.0, LEDs=led_arr)
            self._integrate(dt)
            time.sleep(DT)

    def calibrate_gyro(self):
        """Average gyroscope[2] with the car stationary. Returns True on success."""
        for attempt in range(1, GYRO_CAL_MAX_ATTEMPTS + 1):
            print(f"[GYRO_CAL] hold the car still ({GYRO_CAL_DURATION:.0f} s, attempt {attempt})...")
            samples = []
            t_end = time.monotonic() + GYRO_CAL_DURATION
            while time.monotonic() < t_end and not self._stop:
                self.car.read_write_std(throttle=0.0, steering=0.0, LEDs=leds(brake=True))
                samples.append(float(self.car.gyroscope[2]))
                time.sleep(DT)
            if self._stop:
                return False
            if len(samples) < 10:
                print(f"[GYRO_CAL] only {len(samples)} samples - retrying")
                continue
            mean, std = float(np.mean(samples)), float(np.std(samples))
            if std > GYRO_CAL_MAX_STD:
                print(f"[GYRO_CAL][WARN] noisy: std {std:.4f} rad/s > {GYRO_CAL_MAX_STD:.4f} "
                      f"(car bumped or moving?) - re-running calibration")
                continue
            self.gyro_bias = mean
            print(f"[GYRO_CAL] bias {mean:+.5f} rad/s, std {std:.5f} rad/s ({len(samples)} samples)")
            return True
        self._abort(f"gyro calibration failed {GYRO_CAL_MAX_ATTEMPTS} times "
                    f"(too noisy) - keep the car still and retry")
        return False

    def obstacle_ahead(self, target_speed):
        if target_speed > 0:
            return self.lidar.front() < LIDAR_TO_FRONT_BUMPER + SAFETY_STOP_DIST
        if target_speed < 0:
            return self.lidar.rear() < LIDAR_TO_REAR_BUMPER + SAFETY_STOP_DIST
        return False

    def indicator(self, brake=False):
        return leds(right=self.k == 1, left=self.k == -1, brake=brake)

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------
    # States
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------
    def step_search_vehicles(self):
        side = self.lidar.side(self.k)
        lidar_x = self.odom + LIDAR_FROM_REAR_AXLE
        steer = float(np.clip(K_HEADING * (0.0 - self.heading),
                              -MAX_CORRECTION_STEER, MAX_CORRECTION_STEER))

        if self.odom >= MAX_SEARCH_DISTANCE:
            if self.baseline_side is None:
                self._abort(f"side beam never saw a parked car (closer than "
                            f"{ROW_DETECT_MAX_DIST:.2f} m) within {MAX_SEARCH_DISTANCE:.1f} m")
            elif self.gap_start is not None:
                self._abort(f"no usable gap within {MAX_SEARCH_DISTANCE:.1f} m "
                            f"(a gap was still open, {lidar_x - self.gap_start:.2f} m so far)")
            else:
                self._abort(f"no gap >= {MIN_GAP_WIDTH:.2f} m found within {MAX_SEARCH_DISTANCE:.1f} m")
            return 0.0, 0.0, leds(brake=True)

        if self.baseline_side is None:
            if np.isfinite(side) and side < ROW_DETECT_MAX_DIST:
                self.baseline_side = side
                print(f"[SEARCH] row distance = {side:.2f} m")
            return SEARCH_SPEED, steer, self.indicator()

        is_gap = (not np.isfinite(side)) or (side > self.baseline_side + GAP_DEPTH_JUMP)

        if self.gap_start is None:
            if is_gap:
                self.gap_start = lidar_x
                self.gap_row_dist = self.baseline_side
                print(f"[SEARCH] gap opens at x={self.gap_start:.2f} m")
            else:
                self.baseline_side = 0.9 * self.baseline_side + 0.1 * side
        else:
            width = lidar_x - self.gap_start
            if not is_gap:
                if width >= MIN_GAP_WIDTH:
                    print(f"[SEARCH] gap closes at x={lidar_x:.2f} m, width {width:.2f} m - OK")
                    if self._plan_vehicles(self.gap_start, lidar_x):
                        self.state = "POSITION"
                    else:
                        return 0.0, 0.0, leds(brake=True)
                else:
                    print(f"[SEARCH] gap too narrow ({width:.2f} < {MIN_GAP_WIDTH:.2f} m) - keep looking")
                    self.gap_start = None
                    self.baseline_side = side
            elif width >= MAX_GAP_WIDTH:
                # open space after the last car: use a spot right next to it
                print(f"[SEARCH] open space after x={self.gap_start:.2f} m - using spot beside last vehicle")
                if self._plan_vehicles(self.gap_start, self.gap_start + MIN_GAP_WIDTH + 0.05):
                    self.state = "POSITION"
                else:
                    return 0.0, 0.0, leds(brake=True)

        return SEARCH_SPEED, steer, self.indicator()

    def _stall_search_failure_reason(self):
        d = f"within {MAX_SEARCH_DISTANCE:.1f} m"
        if self.cam_frames == 0:
            return f"no frames received from the {self.side} CSI camera {d}"
        if self.frames_with_lines == 0:
            return (f"no perpendicular tape lines seen in {self.cam_frames} frames {d} "
                    f"(check TAPE_HSV_LOW/HIGH and the BEV with --calibrate-camera)")
        if self.frames_with_stall == 0:
            best = "none" if self.best_spacing is None else f"{self.best_spacing:.2f} m"
            extra = (f"; {self.frames_entrance_cut} frames had a matching pair whose entrance end "
                     f"was outside the camera view") if self.frames_entrance_cut else ""
            return (f"lines seen in {self.frames_with_lines}/{self.cam_frames} frames {d}, but no "
                    f"adjacent pair matched STALL_WIDTH {STALL_WIDTH:.2f} +/- {STALL_WIDTH_TOL:.2f} m "
                    f"(closest spacing seen: {best}){extra}")
        return (f"stall seen in {self.frames_with_stall} frames {d} but never confirmed in "
                f"{STALL_CONFIRM_FRAMES} consecutive frames (best run {self.best_run})")

    def step_search_stall(self):
        steer = float(np.clip(K_HEADING * (0.0 - self.heading),
                              -MAX_CORRECTION_STEER, MAX_CORRECTION_STEER))

        if self.odom >= MAX_SEARCH_DISTANCE:
            self._abort(self._stall_search_failure_reason())
            return 0.0, 0.0, leds(brake=True)

        frame = self.camera.read()
        if frame is None:
            return STALL_SEARCH_SPEED, steer, self.indicator()   # no new frame this loop

        odom_at_frame = self.odom - self.speed * CAMERA_LATENCY_S
        psi = self.heading
        det = self.detector.detect(frame)
        self.cam_frames += 1
        if det["clusters"]:
            self.frames_with_lines += 1
        if det["rejected_entrance"]:
            self.frames_entrance_cut += 1
        for s in det["spacings"]:
            if self.best_spacing is None or abs(s - STALL_WIDTH) < abs(self.best_spacing - STALL_WIDTH):
                self.best_spacing = s

        # car frame -> start frame (odom along the aisle, lateral toward --side).
        # Assumes the car's lateral drift from the start line is ~0 (heading hold).
        cands = []
        for st in det["stalls"]:
            f, out = st["fwd"], st["lateral"]
            x = odom_at_frame + f * math.cos(psi) + self.k * out * math.sin(psi)
            lat = out * math.cos(psi) - self.k * f * math.sin(psi)
            cands.append((x, lat))
        if cands:
            self.frames_with_stall += 1

        match = None
        if self.stall_track:
            mx = float(np.mean([t[0] for t in self.stall_track]))
            ml = float(np.mean([t[1] for t in self.stall_track]))
            close = [c for c in cands
                     if abs(c[0] - mx) <= STALL_MATCH_TOL and abs(c[1] - ml) <= STALL_MATCH_TOL_LATERAL]
            if close:
                match = min(close, key=lambda c: abs(c[0] - mx))
            else:
                self.stall_misses += 1
                if self.stall_misses > STALL_MAX_MISSES:
                    self.stall_track = []
                    self.stall_misses = 0
        if match is None and not self.stall_track and cands:
            match = min(cands, key=lambda c: c[0])      # start tracking the nearest-along-aisle stall

        if match is not None:
            self.stall_track.append(match)
            self.stall_misses = 0
            self.best_run = max(self.best_run, len(self.stall_track))
            print(f"[SEARCH] stall candidate x={match[0]:.2f} m, lateral={match[1]:.2f} m "
                  f"({len(self.stall_track)}/{STALL_CONFIRM_FRAMES})")

        if len(self.stall_track) >= STALL_CONFIRM_FRAMES:
            xs = np.array([t[0] for t in self.stall_track])
            ls = np.array([t[1] for t in self.stall_track])
            print(f"[SEARCH] stall confirmed: x={xs.mean():.3f} m (std {xs.std():.3f}), "
                  f"lateral={ls.mean():.3f} m (std {ls.std():.3f}) over {len(xs)} frames")
            self._plan_empty(float(xs.mean()), float(ls.mean()))
            self.state = "POSITION"

        return STALL_SEARCH_SPEED, steer, self.indicator()

    def step_position(self):
        err = self.turn_start_x - self.odom
        if abs(err) < 0.01:
            self.stop_car(self.indicator(brake=True), settle=0.5)
            self.turn_start_odom = self.odom
            self.state = "TURN"
            print(f"[POSITION] at turn point (heading {math.degrees(self.heading):.1f} deg) - turning")
            return 0.0, 0.0, self.indicator(brake=True)
        speed = math.copysign(POSITION_SPEED if abs(err) > 0.10 else 0.06, err)
        steer = K_HEADING * (0.0 - self.heading) * (1 if speed > 0 else -1)
        steer = float(np.clip(steer, -MAX_CORRECTION_STEER, MAX_CORRECTION_STEER))
        return speed, steer, self.indicator()

    def step_turn(self):
        travelled = abs(self.odom - self.turn_start_odom)
        expected_arc = TURN_RADIUS * math.pi / 2.0
        reached = abs(self.heading) >= abs(self.target_heading) - math.radians(2.0)
        if reached or travelled > TURN_ARC_TOLERANCE * expected_arc:
            if not reached:
                print(f"[WARN] arc length exceeded, heading only {math.degrees(self.heading):.1f} deg")
            self.stop_car(self.indicator(brake=True), settle=0.3)
            self.enter_start_odom = self.odom
            self.state = "ENTER"
            print(f"[TURN] done, heading {math.degrees(self.heading):.1f} deg - entering spot")
            return 0.0, 0.0, self.indicator(brake=True)
        # steer toward the spot side for both entry directions
        return self.dir * TURN_SPEED, -self.k * MAX_STEER, self.indicator()

    def step_enter(self):
        travelled = abs(self.odom - self.enter_start_odom)
        if travelled >= self.entry_depth:
            self.state = "DONE"
            return 0.0, 0.0, leds(brake=True)

        err_h = self.target_heading - self.heading
        steer = self.dir * K_HEADING * err_h

        if self.mode == "vehicles":
            left = self.lidar.sector(90.0, 10.0)
            right = self.lidar.sector(-90.0, 10.0)
            if np.isfinite(left) and np.isfinite(right) and left < 0.5 and right < 0.5:
                # positive -> car is too far right -> move left (+ steer works for both directions)
                lateral_err = 0.5 * (left - right)
                steer += K_CENTER * lateral_err

        steer = float(np.clip(steer, -MAX_CORRECTION_STEER, MAX_CORRECTION_STEER))
        return self.dir * ENTER_SPEED, steer, leds()

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------
    # Main loop
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------
    def run(self):
        print(f"Perpendicular parking | mode={self.mode} entry={self.entry} "
              f"side={self.side} | Ctrl+C to abort")
        steps = {
            "SEARCH": self.step_search_vehicles if self.mode == "vehicles" else self.step_search_stall,
            "POSITION": self.step_position,
            "TURN": self.step_turn,
            "ENTER": self.step_enter,
        }
        try:
            if not self.calibrate_gyro():
                return
            self.heading = 0.0
            self.odom = 0.0
            self._last_t = time.monotonic()

            t0 = time.monotonic()
            prev_loop = t0
            log_t = t0
            loop_times = []

            while not self._stop and self.state not in ("DONE", "ABORT"):
                loop_start = time.monotonic()
                loop_times.append(loop_start - prev_loop)
                prev_loop = loop_start
                if loop_start - log_t >= TIMING_LOG_PERIOD and loop_times:
                    print(f"[TIMING] loop avg {1000 * np.mean(loop_times):.1f} ms, "
                          f"max {1000 * np.max(loop_times):.1f} ms "
                          f"({len(loop_times)} iterations) | state {self.state} | "
                          f"odom {self.odom:+.3f} m, heading {math.degrees(self.heading):+.1f} deg")
                    loop_times = []
                    log_t = loop_start

                if loop_start - t0 > MAX_RUN_TIME:
                    print("[!] timeout")
                    break

                self.lidar.update()
                target_speed, steer, led_arr = steps[self.state]()

                if self.obstacle_ahead(target_speed):
                    if self.state == "ENTER":
                        # curb / wall at the back (or front) of the spot - we're in
                        print("[ENTER] reached end of spot")
                        self.state = "DONE"
                    else:
                        print(f"[SAFETY] obstacle in path during {self.state} - holding")
                    target_speed = 0.0
                    led_arr = leds(brake=True)

                self.drive(target_speed, steer, led_arr)

                elapsed = time.monotonic() - loop_start
                if elapsed < DT:
                    time.sleep(DT - elapsed)

            if self.state == "DONE":
                self.lidar.update()
                print(f"[DONE] parked. heading error "
                      f"{math.degrees(self.heading - self.target_heading):+.1f} deg | "
                      f"left {self.lidar.sector(90, 10):.2f} m, right {self.lidar.sector(-90, 10):.2f} m")
            elif self.state == "ABORT":
                print(f"[ABORT] stopped without parking: {self.abort_reason}")
        finally:
            self.stop_car(leds(left=True, right=True, brake=True))   # hazards
            self.car.terminate()
            self.lidar.terminate()
            if self.camera is not None:
                self.camera.terminate()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Calibration modes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def calibrate():
    """Print sector distances so you can confirm FRONT_ANGLE_DEG / ANGLE_DIR."""
    lidar = LidarView()
    print("Hold an object at the front / right / rear / left of the car. Ctrl+C to quit.")
    try:
        while True:
            lidar.update()
            print(f"front {lidar.sector(0, 10):5.2f}  "
                  f"left {lidar.sector(90, 10):5.2f}  "
                  f"rear {lidar.sector(180, 10):5.2f}  "
                  f"right {lidar.sector(-90, 10):5.2f}   [m]", end="\r")
            time.sleep(0.1)
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        print()
    finally:
        lidar.terminate()


def calibrate_camera(side):
    """Save sample frames (car does not move) so tape thresholds / BEV can be tuned:
         NN_undistorted.png  undistorted PROC_SIZE frame (use this to pick homography points)
         NN_bev_overlay.png  bird's-eye view with red = all Hough segments,
                             green = perpendicular segments, blue = merged tape lines
                             (cyan dot = entrance end visible, red dot = cut off),
                             yellow circle = detected stall center
         NN_mask.png         tape threshold mask in the bird's-eye view
    """
    detector = StallLineDetector(side)
    camera = SideCamera(side, dedupe=False)
    os.makedirs(CAMCAL_OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)
    print(f"Saving {CAMCAL_NUM_FRAMES} frames from the {side} camera to {CAMCAL_OUTPUT_DIR} "
          f"every {CAMCAL_INTERVAL:.1f} s. The car will not move. Ctrl+C to stop.")
    saved = 0
    next_t = time.monotonic()
    try:
        while saved < CAMCAL_NUM_FRAMES:
            frame = camera.read()
            if frame is None or time.monotonic() < next_t:
                time.sleep(0.01)
                continue
            next_t += CAMCAL_INTERVAL
            det = detector.detect(frame)
            base = os.path.join(CAMCAL_OUTPUT_DIR, f"{saved:02d}")
            cv2.imwrite(base + "_undistorted.png", detector.undistort(det["small"]))
            cv2.imwrite(base + "_bev_overlay.png", detector.draw(det))
            cv2.imwrite(base + "_mask.png", det["mask"])
            lines = ", ".join(f"{c['fwd']:+.2f}{'' if c['entrance_visible'] else '(cut)'}"
                              for c in det["clusters"]) or "none"
            stalls = ", ".join(f"(fwd {s['fwd']:+.2f}, lateral {s['lateral']:.2f}, "
                               f"spacing {s['spacing']:.2f})" for s in det["stalls"]) or "none"
            print(f"[{saved:02d}] segments {len(det['segs'])}, perpendicular {len(det['kept'])} | "
                  f"lines at fwd [m]: {lines} | stalls: {stalls}")
            saved += 1
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        print()
    finally:
        camera.terminate()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="QCar 1 autonomous perpendicular parking")
    ap.add_argument("--mode", choices=["vehicles", "empty"], default="vehicles",
                    help="vehicles: find a gap between parked cars (LiDAR); "
                         "empty: find a taped stall in an empty lot (side camera)")
    ap.add_argument("--entry", choices=["reverse", "forward"], default="reverse",
                    help="back into the spot (default) or drive in nose first")
    ap.add_argument("--side", choices=["right", "left"], default="right",
                    help="which side of the aisle the spot is on (also selects the camera)")
    ap.add_argument("--calibrate", action="store_true",
                    help="print LiDAR sector distances without moving the car")
    ap.add_argument("--calibrate-camera", action="store_true",
                    help="save bird's-eye frames with detected lines for the --side camera "
                         "without moving the car")
    args = ap.parse_args()

    if args.calibrate:
        calibrate()
    elif args.calibrate_camera:
        calibrate_camera(args.side)
    else:
        PerpendicularParker(args.mode, args.entry, args.side).run()
    sys.exit(0)
